six (P=0.120 on fc2 -- most flagged growth is wrong), and wind_run actually edges it on F1. IMPORTANT CAVEAT: arrival_run trained on the leaky 'observed' corpus (crop centered/sized on t0|t1, i.e. it saw the future perimeter's geometry during training) and has NEVER seen a t0-window crop -- the ONLY geometry this live pipeline can ever produce at forecast time (the future perimeter is, by definition, unknown). So every live prediction from this model is out-of-distribution relative to its own training. The measured t0-window numbers above already reflect that (they are not a surprise), but this is 'best available', not 'production-ready' -- represent it that way. The operating_point (floor=0.0, mult=0.9) is the VAL-selected connected-causal decode point; it did NOT clear the 0.50 precision floor during selection (feasible=False, val P=0.270/R=0.259) -- it's the best-F1 fallback point, not a precision-guaranteed one.","issued_at_utc":"2026-07-25 02:03:51.594413+00:00","valid_from_utc":"2026-07-24 00:00:00","valid_to_utc":"2026-07-25 00:00:00","wfigs_date_current_utc":"2026-07-24 22:20:00+00:00","pixel_size_m":30,"veg_source":"refreshed_d4","physics_source":"eikonal_fbfm40","history_n_dates":2,"degraded_history":false,"containment_pct":69,"acres_wfigs":3042.1169078799,"hour":15,"valid_at_utc":"2026-07-24 15:00:00"}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-108.21218,40.21087],[-108.21147,40.21087],[-108.21147,40.2106],[-108.21218,40.2106],[-108.21218,40.21087]]],[[[-108.21606,40.2203],[-108.21571,40.2203],[-108.21571,40.22003],[-108.21606,40.22003],[-108.21606,40.2203]]],[[[-108.21924,40.22758],[-108.21924,40.22731],[-108.21889,40.22731],[-108.21889,40.22677],[-108.21818,40.22677],[-108.21818,40.22623],[-108.21747,40.22596],[-108.21747,40.22542],[-108.21677,40.22515],[-108.21677,40.22407],[-108.21712,40.22407],[-108.21712,40.22273],[-108.21747,40.22273],[-108.21747,40.22219],[-108.21712,40.22219],[-108.21712,40.22165],[-108.21747,40.22165